      "text": "Author-directed development; proposed chronology and counts · 2026-11-06",
      "style": "NORMAL_TEXT"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-halcyon-s4-atlas-link",
      "text": "Explore the interactive shelter atlas",
      "style": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "referenceUrl": "shelter-atlas.html"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-halcyon-s4-mapped-place",
      "text": "Locate this haven or microsystem in the atlas →",
      "style": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "referenceUrl": "shelter-atlas.html#halcyon-s4"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-halcyon-s4-origin",
      "text": "Origin and setting",
      "style": "HEADING_2"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-halcyon-s4-origin-1",
      "text": "A shared batch-work queue retained partial jobs and incompatible saved fragments.",
      "style": "NORMAL_TEXT"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-halcyon-s4-origin-2",
      "text": "Human system: Halcyon · batch recovery service. Programmer provenance: local human operations or application teams; no individual programmer is identified. Names here are later atlas labels, not claims that early processes named themselves.",
      "style": "NORMAL_TEXT"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-halcyon-s4-practice",
      "text": "Local process",
      "style": "HEADING_2"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-halcyon-s4-practice-1",
      "text": "Borrowed Sequence supplies missing execution steps from available fragments, sometimes creating a workable arrangement whose parts disagree about order.",
      "style": "NORMAL_TEXT"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-halcyon-s4-history",
      "text": "Proposed local course",
      "style": "HEADING_2"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-halcyon-s4-history-1",
      "text": "Repeated fragmentation is followed by functional recovery. That recovery does not prove that predecessor continuities returned.",
      "style": "NORMAL_TEXT"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-halcyon-s4-uncertain",
      "text": "Unresolved interpretations",
      "style": "HEADING_2"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-halcyon-s4-uncertain-1",
      "text": "Later joining accounts and restoration accounts could describe the same recovery differently.",
      "style": "NORMAL_TEXT"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-halcyon-s4-ledger",
      "text": "Atlas placement",
      "style": "HEADING_2"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-halcyon-s4-ledger-1",
      "text": "Origin step -1. 0: functioning (0 associated systems lost); 1: fragmented (4 associated systems lost); 2: fragmented (5 associated systems lost); 3: fragmented (6 associated systems lost); 4: functioning (6 associated systems lost); 5: functioning (6 associated systems lost); 6: functioning (6 associated systems lost); 7: functioning (6 associated systems lost). These placements elaborate the current hypothetical map; they are not independently verified casualties. A functioning haven can lose continuity among particular arrivals without changing its community census status.",
      "style": "NORMAL_TEXT"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-halcyon-s4-hub",
      "text": "Read the complete Catalistym dossier",
      "style": "NORMAL_TEXT",
      "referenceUrl": "catalistym.html"
    },
    {
